        content: "**Effects of Smoke on the Respiratory System**\\n\\nSmoke, whether from tobacco, biomass burning, or environmental pollution, contains thousands of harmful chemicals.\\n\\n**Immediate Effects:**\\n• Irritation of the airways, causing coughing\\n• Constriction of air passages (bronchospasm)\\n• Increased mucus production\\n• Reduced function of cilia (tiny hairs that sweep mucus upward)\\n\\n**Long-term Effects:**\\n• Chronic bronchitis — persistent inflammation of the bronchi\\n• Emphysema — damage and destruction of alveoli\\n• Lung cancer — uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells\\n• Reduced lung function and breathlessness\\n\\n**Key dangerous chemicals in tobacco smoke:**\\n• **Nicotine** — addictive substance\\n• **Tar** — carcinogenic (cancer-causing)\\n• **Carbon monoxide** — reduces oxygen-carrying capacity of blood\\n• **Formaldehyde** — toxic and irritating",
