        content: "**Applications in Transportation**\\n\\n**1. Ships and Boats:**\\n• Ships are designed with large hollow hulls to displace maximum water\\n• The shape of the hull determines stability and efficiency\\n• Different types of ships (cargo, tanker, passenger) have different designs\\n\\n**2. Submarines:**\\n• Submarines use ballast tanks to control buoyancy\\n• To dive: fill tanks with water (increase density)\\n• To surface: fill tanks with air (decrease density)\\n• Neutral buoyancy maintains a constant depth\\n\\n**3. Life Jackets:**\\n• Made from buoyant materials (foam or inflatable chambers)\\n• Provide additional buoyancy to keep a person's head above water\\n\\n**4. Hot Air Balloons:**\\n• Operate on the same principle but in air (a fluid)\\n• Hot air is less dense than cool air → balloon rises\\n• To descend: let the air cool or release hot air",
